  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts with the pyramid scene. It passes the typecheck, but I couldn't run it in a browser, so none of the behavior below has been seen. Physics, the launch, the Space reset and the shadows are untested.\n\n- **Scene:** 15 dynamic boxes in rows of 5, 4, 3, 2 and 1 sit on a static floor, with real rigid-body physics (`physics: { bindNodes: true }`). The lighting is a neutral environment plus a shadow-casting directional light, and the boxes, ball and floor cast and receive shadows. The camera is a perspective view from the side that takes in the pyramid and the ball's path.\n- **Launch:** the ball starts about 11 units in front of the pyramid. After 1.5 s of simulated time it gets a velocity of 24 units/s toward the pyramid. Physics steps at a fixed 1/60 s inside `app.onFrame`.\n- **Reset:** Space rebuilds the scene with `app.setScene`, restarts the 1.5 s timer and relaunches. I used `setScene` because the physics body handles can't reset a body's rotation, so the tumbled boxes couldn't be put back upright any other way. The engine's own notes advise against `setScene` for restarts, so this is the most likely thing to need a check.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` and two animation frames. I avoided top-level `await` so `vite build` doesn't trip on its default browser target.\n- **Canvas:** `createAuraApp` draws into the existing `#app` canvas.\n\n",
